# The upstream commits the interim producer (run-producer.sh) is proven against.
# One line per upstream directory: <directory> <full commit>.
# lib/sidestr-upstream.nix bakes these commits into the image (/opt/agentbox/sidestr/upstream)
# and evaluation fails when its rev and hash do not match the line here; the runner refuses a
# bake whose recorded .pin-commit differs. Bump a line only after the chain has been restarted
# and a block produced on that commit, which means a run from a checkout under
# SIDESTR_ALLOW_UNPINNED=1 first, then this line, the rev and hash, and a rebuild. sidestr-rs's CI oracle job pins its own spec commit (e8deb63, SPEC 0.0.5, SIDESTR_SPEC_REF), not this one.
